   "properties": {
    "content_rating": "TV-MA",
    "description": "Money Heist (original Spanish title La Casa de Papel) is a 2017 crime-thriller television series created by Álex Pina. Centered on a master planner who recruits a ragtag team of thieves identified by city codenames, the series chronicles an elaborate takeover of Spain's Royal Mint and its aftermath. With a large ensemble cast led by Álvaro Morte and Úrsula Corberó alongside Itziar Ituño, Pedro Alonso, Alba Flores, Miguel Herrán and others, the show blends pulse-pounding heist mechanics with intimate character backstories, romance, and ideological conflict. Visually bold and fast-paced, the series explores themes of class struggle, loyalty, identity, media spectacle and the ethics of resistance while maintaining a tense, emotionally charged tone that balances spectacle and character-driven drama.",
