   ],
   "properties": {
    "content_rating": "TV-MA",
    "description": "Money Heist: Korea - Joint Economic Area (2022), directed by Kim Hong-sun, is a South Korean adaptation of the international heist format built around a mastermind who engineers an audacious takeover of the national mint on a newly unified peninsula. The ensemble cast includes Yoo Ji-tae, Park Hae-soo and Jeon Jong-seo among others. Framed as a heist and crime drama with thriller and action subcurrents, the series follows the planners inside the mint and the crisis negotiation and police teams outside as tactical gambits, interpersonal conflicts and political pressures escalate. The narrative foregrounds strategic ingenuity and ensemble dynamics while probing themes of economic disparity, identity and moral ambiguity. Tonally it oscillates between pulse-pounding suspense and quieter, character-driven drama, presented in a stylized, cinematic visual language that draws on Korean noir sensibilities and high-octane execution.",
